{"name":"Sacred Sapling","hex":"#7c8635","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"sacred","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Characterized by solemn religious ceremony or religious use, especially, in a positive sense; consecrated, made holy.","Religious; relating to religion, or to the services of religion; not secular"]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["simple past and past participle of sacre"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sacred"},{"term":"sapling","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A young tree, larger than a seedling.","A youngster, especially a male nearing maturity."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sapling"}],"entries":[{"title":"Sacredness","blocks":[{"text":"Sacred describes something that is dedicated or set apart for the service or worship of a deity; is considered worthy of spiritual respect or devotion; or inspires awe or reverence among believers. The property is often ascribed to objects, or places."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sacredness","wikidata":"Q1151419"},{"title":"Tree","blocks":[{"text":"In botany, a tree is a perennial plant with an elongated stem, or trunk, usually supporting branches and leaves. In some usages, the definition of a tree may be narrower, e.g., including only woody plants with secondary growth, only plants that are usable for timber, or only plants above a specified height. Wider definitions include taller palms, tree ferns, bananas, and bamboos."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7f/Usamljeni_jasen_-_panoramio_%28cropped%29.jpg/330px-Usamljeni_jasen_-_panoramio_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tree","wikidata":"Q10884"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/14/High_Priest_Offering_Sacrifice_of_a_Goat.jpg/500px-High_Priest_Offering_Sacrifice_of_a_Goat.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia